Trip troubleshooting script:
US/Japanese version of trip troubleshooting plan:
1、 R1/R2/MX16 US version tripped:
1. Unplug other power cords that are plugged into the same row as the treadmill; If the power cord of other appliances is unplugged and does not trip, it indicates that the working current is greater than the rated protection current of the circuit breaker (15A/20A/30A);
2. After checking the first item, it still tripped and the grounding copper strip was cancelled; If it does not trip, it indicates that the leakage current is greater than 5mA, causing the circuit breaker to trip;
3. Replace the grounding copper strip with a resistive grounding;
2、 Z1/R3/Z3/X218 US version tripped:
1. Unplug other power cords that are plugged into the same row as the treadmill; If the power cord of other appliances is unplugged and does not trip, it indicates that the working current is greater than the rated protection current of the circuit breaker; （15A/20A/30A）；
2. After checking the first item, it still tripped and the grounding copper strip was cancelled; If it does not trip, it indicates that the leakage current is greater than 5mA, causing the circuit breaker to trip;
3、 European trip:
1. The MX16 series/Z1/R3/Z3/X218 motors have grounding wires or copper grounding plates. Remove one end of the grounding wire of the motor or remove the grounding copper plate;
2. After troubleshooting the first item, if it still trips, please contact technical support

